# Context

## Why This Way
The checkpoint gate was a hard-coded literal 6 at three mirror
sites (legality, observation, policy). Making it rule data lets
the same frozen policy ladder measure any threshold without code
changes; the default keeps every existing rules file bit-identical
in behavior (verified: baseline and C2 replay 0/480 winner drift).

## Gotchas
- Lowering the threshold implicitly shortens phase 1 through the
  grace-round trigger: first claim at ~round 10 vs ~17 means the
  whole game tempo changes, not just the gate. Any retry should
  adjust grace_full_rounds together with the requirement.
- The set-completion reward only fires for players who collect
  all six; with phase 1 ending early, that is 64 awards in 480
  games. A reward nobody reaches is not a trade-off.
